  "id": "COMPOUND:25521 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "Asaraldehyde is implicated in the interaction with SN12K1 through multiple pathways, with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex serving as a common intermediary in two of the three paths. In Path 1, Asaraldehyde targets NAD-dependent protein deacetylase sirtuin-2, which in turn targets Eurostoside, ultimately leading to SN12K1. In Path 2 and 3, Asaraldehyde directly targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which then targets Rha(a1-3)[coumaroyl(3-OH)(-4)]Glc(b)-O-EtPh and Docosanoic acid, pentyl ester, both of which also target SN12K1. The shared involvement of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex across these pathways suggests a potential mechanism involving histone modification or chromatin regulation. The evidence supports a role for Asaraldehyde in modulating the activity of this complex, which in turn influences SN12K1. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex for SN12K1 regulation, with Asaraldehyde acting as a modulator of this pathway. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Asaraldehyde influences the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which then affects SN12K1 through a common target.",
